data/


# WSL/cmd HOME-path accident: never commit a literal Windows home tree into the repo
C:*
web/C:*
*Carter*

# Generated project-context brain/map (rebuilt by the worker; not source)
Advisory.said
PROJECT_CONTEXT.md

# said binaries are large compiled artifacts — build/copy locally, do not commit (see tools/said/README.md).
# Ignore every binary under tools/said (both .exe and -linux) but KEEP the tracked README.
tools/said/*
!tools/said/README.md
.claude-worker/
# Bulk vulnerability feeds — we query VulnCheck/MITRE ONLINE (api.vulncheck.com via VULNCHECK_API_KEY),
# so these local dumps are unused. They are also far over GitHub's 100 MB file limit (mitre-cve.json is
# ~1.5 GB) and would break any push that included them.
vulncheck_known_exploited_vulnerabilities.json
mitre-cve.json
Vulncheck/
.tmp-pip-test/
advisory-rollout-*.tar.gz

# IT handoff bundle (contains live keys — never commit)
handoff/

# local archive / build artifact (33 MB) — not versioned
Advisory.zip
